<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis falls on weak demand.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis falls on weak demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean meal basis offers in U.S. cash markets were lower on Tuesday as buyers held out for cheaper January prices and export demand remained slack, several cash brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The cash movement has been nil,&quot; an Indiana broker said. &quot;In January we should start to see some good movement.&quot;</p>
<p>Most locations continued to quote basis values versus the CBOT December contract which was trading at a $10 per ton premium to the January.</p>
<p>However, one Chicago processor reportedly shifted to the January and carried about $8 of the spread, brokers said.</p>
<p>Several sources noted South American growing conditions were ideal which supported ideas of abundant world soybean supplies next spring.  </p>
